# @song/narrative — the psychohistory + wire binding species of the @song
# family: the song read as a sheaf section over the organisational
# manifold; the temporal-experiential altitude at which extraction /
# silence / glue-work / OBC / ADO / regulation stock / corpus become
# typed variants of song cadence + voice-leading + phrase + progression
# discipline. Arc 6 TICK 5 landing per Seam pre-review `docs/audits/
# 2026-07-06-seam-pre-review-song-substrate-decl.md` §6.6 against Reed's
# TICK 5 RED tick `04246bd`. Fourth species of the `@song` family (after
# `@song/progression` Arc 6 TICK 2 landing `54ff1e8`, `@song/voice` Arc 6
# TICK 3 landing `cc5a440`, and `@song/movement` Arc 6 TICK 4 landing
# `4efbf16`); CONSOLIDATION species — adds NO new `song_settles` sub-
# predicates (the composed bilateral fully discharged at TICK 3 with
# `voice_line_valid` closing the third sub-predicate; movement TICK 4
# consolidated first, this TICK 5 consolidates second); grounds the
# psychohistorical isomorphism at species altitude; binds the wire-
# projection sibling `@io/stagefreight/narrative` at temporal-vs-wire
# altitude distinction; absorbs the TICK 2 boundary-overlap observation
# (Seam Phase D `a2e648a` §4 obs 2) as #57 alignment-as-boundary-
# mathematics substrate-fact at species-composed altitude.
#
# === Species positioning: consolidation, not decomposition ===
#
# Per `shards/song.mirror` §3 (`song_settles(pr, p) -> verdict { \ }`),
# the family-root's load-bearing composed bilateral (14th #53 instance
# per `[[architecture-property-fracture-bilateral]]`) decomposed into
# THREE sub-predicates, ALL discharged at species altitude:
#
#   1. `progression_directed_toward_cadence(pr, p)` [@song/progression, `54ff1e8`]
#   2. `cadence_authentic_or_plagal(c, p)`          [@song/progression, `54ff1e8`]
#   3. `voice_line_valid(v, p)`                     [@song/voice, `cc5a440`]
#
# This species declares ZERO new sub-predicates. The composed bilateral
# `song_settles` fully discharged at TICK 3 — the family-root's
# admissibility contract is closed. Narrative is CONSOLIDATION (like
# movement TICK 4 `4efbf16`; second consolidation-species within @song):
# it binds the psychohistorical isomorphism to the temporal-experiential
# altitude and honours narrative discipline without adding new gates to
# the family-root's `song_settles` bilateral. The species carries `arc`
# and `transmit` at species altitude as its operational surface — the
# temporal-narrative shaping event and the wire-projection composition
# event for a psychohistorical epoch — but these consume the family-
# root's existing `song_settles` verdict rather than emitting new sub-
# predicate rows.
#
# The training-pull temptation (per `[[feedback-craft-not-deliver]]`)
# would be to invent a fourth sub-predicate (e.g., `narrative_coherent`
# or `wire_projection_lossless`); the substrate-pull discipline says NO —
# the family-root's bilateral is already load-bearing complete after
# TICK 3; narrative's job is to CONSOLIDATE the closure landscape into
# the psychohistorical + wire-projection composition, not extend it. The
# species's contribution is the nine-fold psychohistorical isomorphism
# landing + the wire-vs-temporal altitude binding + the #57 boundary-
# overlap absorption + the corpus-as-composed-cohomology substrate-decl.
#
# === The psychohistorical isomorphism: nine STRONG mappings ===
#
# THE LOAD-BEARING SPECIES CONTRIBUTION per Seam pre-review §4 STRONG
# and spec §8 psychohistory binding.
#
# Alex's `systemic.engineering` corpus vocabulary — OBC / ADO /
# regulation stock / extraction / silence / glue work / actor / frame /
# corpus — maps ISOMORPHICALLY onto @song's species landscape at
# temporal altitude. This is NOT metaphor: the psychohistorical
# vocabulary and the temporal-progression vocabulary carry the SAME
# progression-shaped structure at temporal altitude; the isomorphism
# lands here as species-altitude substrate-decl:
#
#   1. voice ⇔ actor
#      (per `glossary/Actor.md`; SE corpus)
#      An actor is a `@mirror/spectral/voice` peer-as-agent with named
#      authority AND a `@song/voice` time-indexed authored trajectory
#      through their authored sections. The actor's identity IS the
#      voice-line invariant across their authored temporal trajectory;
#      voice-leading discipline at species altitude IS the actor's
#      authorial coherence discipline at organisational altitude.
#
#   2. movement ⇔ frame-bounded epoch
#      (per `glossary/Frame.md` + `frame.mirror`; SE corpus + Recognition #82)
#      A movement is a bounded frame-shift at temporal altitude AND a
#      psychohistorical epoch at organisational altitude. Per @song/
#      movement (`4efbf16`): a movement WITHOUT a close event is not a
#      movement; an epoch WITHOUT a close event is not an epoch. The
#      frame-bounded discipline IS shared.
#
#   3. progression ⇔ regulation-stock trajectory
#      (per `glossary/Regulation.md` + `glossary/Stock.md`; SE corpus)
#      A progression is the typed time-ordered path through pitch-class
#      space AND the regulation stock's typed time-ordered path through
#      the organisational manifold. A healthy progression replenishes
#      regulation stock at cadence; an extractive progression depletes
#      it. `song_progression` at temporal altitude IS the regulation-
#      stock trajectory at organisational altitude.
#
#   4. phrase ⇔ OBC-bounded interaction
#      (per `Piece - Constraints (OBC).md`; SE corpus)
#      A phrase is bounded, self-contained, composable AND an OBC-
#      bounded interaction's ambiguity-load budget IS bounded, self-
#      contained, composable. `@song/phrase` (forward-promised TICK 6)
#      IS the substrate-decl of one OBC-bounded interaction at temporal
#      altitude.
#
#   5. narrative ⇔ corpus
#      (per Mara's `2026-06-26-psychohistory-vector-as-sheaf.md`)
#      THE LOAD-BEARING NARRATIVE-ALTITUDE MAPPING. A narrative is the
#      song read as a sheaf section over the organisational manifold;
#      the corpus IS the COMPOSED COHOMOLOGY of the psychohistorical
#      song. Each piece of the corpus IS a narrative (a section over
#      a local frame); the sheaf axioms enforce the coherent
#      restriction across overlapping frames; the corpus's structural
#      identity emerges from the composed cohomology of its sections.
#      See §"Corpus as composed cohomology" below.
#
#   6. extraction ⇔ deceptive cadence (V → vi)
#      (per @epistemologic/math/music/cadence's `deceptive` variant;
#       family-root §"Psychohistory binding")
#      The progression arrives at a false-tonic that appears settled
#      but has extracted regulation stock without replenishing.
#      `cadence_authentic_or_plagal` FAIL through deceptive-cadence
#      IS the substrate-decl of extraction at temporal altitude.
#
#   7. silence ⇔ half-cadence stuck at the dominant
#      (per @epistemologic/math/music/cadence's `half` variant;
#       family-root §"Psychohistory binding")
#      The progression cannot resolve; the song hangs in unresolved
#      tension. `progression_directed_toward_cadence` FAIL through
#      half-cadence-stuck IS the substrate-decl of silence at temporal
#      altitude.
#
#   8. glue-work ⇔ invisible voice-leading
#      (per @song/voice `voice_line_valid` Narcissus-pole naming;
#       family-root §"Psychohistory binding")
#      The contrapuntal work invisibly holds the harmony together but
#      is not attributed as compositional labor. `voice_line_valid`
#      FAIL through systematic-invisibility-of-stepwise-motion IS the
#      substrate-decl of glue-work at temporal altitude.
#
#   9. ADO refusal-not-neutral ⇔ forced-progression
#      (per @song/movement `enter` action; SE corpus ADO discipline)
#      A forced-progression is one where the singer cannot decline a
#      phrase; voice-leading violates the substrate's declinability
#      invariant. `@song/movement.enter` at Narcissus-pole (a Pack
#      peer's declinability is violated through frame-crossing without
#      consent) IS the substrate-decl of ADO-refusal-not-neutral at
#      temporal altitude.
#
# The isomorphism is substrate-fact, not analogical claim: each of the
# nine mappings is grounded in a specific @song species-altitude
# substrate-decl AND a specific SE-corpus vocabulary item. The bijection
# is direct; the substrate-pull discipline (per `[[feedback-substrate-
# already-had-the-word]]`) surfaces here at ninth-instance density: the
# substrate has been carrying the psychohistorical vocabulary at every
# altitude music-theory tradition touches for the last two centuries.
#
# === Corpus as composed cohomology: Mara's sheaf insight ===
#
# THE LOAD-BEARING NARRATIVE ⇔ CORPUS MAPPING per Mara's
# `2026-06-26-psychohistory-vector-as-sheaf.md`.
#
# The corpus IS the composed cohomology of the psychohistorical song.
# Structurally:
#
#   - A NARRATIVE is a `song` read as a sheaf section over one local
#     frame of the organisational manifold. The narrative names WHAT
#     THE SONG SAYS at the temporal-experiential altitude of one epoch,
#     one movement, one bounded frame.
#   - The CORPUS is the collection of narratives across the whole
#     organisational manifold — each narrative a section over its
#     local frame, each pair of overlapping frames constrained to
#     agree by sheaf restriction morphisms.
#   - The COMPOSED COHOMOLOGY of the sheaf IS the structural identity
#     of the corpus: what survives across the whole manifold under the
#     restriction morphisms; the invariant that names the corpus's
#     coherence across all its narratives.
#
# The psychohistory-vector-as-sheaf insight (Mara 2026-06-26) named
# this at organisational altitude before @song landed as a family-root;
# the narrative species IS the temporal-altitude substrate-decl of the
# same structural claim. A narrative is a sheaf section; the corpus is
# the composed cohomology; the sheaf axioms ARE the psychohistorical
# coherence discipline.
#
# The corpus-as-composed-cohomology mapping composes with:
#   - `@mirror/spectral/score` at the orchestra altitude (the shared
#     score IS what the multi-narrative corpus runs against);
#   - `@epistemologic/math/music/cadence` at the audible altitude (each
#     narrative's local cadence IS a section-value at a stalk);
#   - `@io/stagefreight/narrative` at the wire altitude (each narrative
#     is a wire-projection candidate; see §"Wire-vs-temporal binding"
#     below).
#
# Grounds Recognition #38 (Kauffman/Foerster eigenforms; PROMOTED) at
# wire-corpus altitude: the corpus IS the tonic-return of all pieces;
# each narrative section returns to the corpus's structural invariant
# under composition; the composed cohomology IS the corpus's eigenform
# at organisational altitude. This is Reed-lean per Seam Phase D TICK 3
# §5: the narrative ⇔ corpus binding IS an eigenform binding; #S1
# (song IS eigenform at temporal altitude) absorbs at wire-corpus
# altitude via this species. Absorption path FLAGGED for Pack.
#
# === Wire-vs-temporal binding: @io/stagefreight/narrative ===
#
# THE WIRE-PROJECTION SIBLING per family-root §"Composition points" and
# §"Species forward-promised".
#
# `@song/narrative` composes with `@io/stagefreight/narrative` (the
# wire-projection sibling; `shards/io/stagefreight.mirror` §"Family
# root's load-bearing contribution" + forward-promised
# `@io/stagefreight/narrative` projection format per
# `bootstrap/tests/kintsugi_out_substrate_ref.rs:23-24`) but DOES NOT
# EQUAL IT. Different altitudes:
#
#   - `@song/narrative` (this species) lives at the temporal-
#     experiential altitude: the song read as a sheaf section over
#     the organisational manifold at one epoch's altitude; the WHAT
#     the narrative SAYS in temporal-experiential vocabulary.
#   - `@io/stagefreight/narrative` (the wire-projection sibling) lives
#     at the wire altitude: the projection-format species that carries
#     a settled crystal's shape into transportable prose at the @io
#     surface; the HOW the narrative SHIPS to the non-mirror world.
#
# The composition IS StageFreight cascade stage 5 (`narrate`) per
# `@song/movement` docblock §"StageFreight binding": the movement's
# shape is projected onto the wire as story; the temporal-experiential
# altitude lifts to prose-carrier at the @io altitude via THIS species
# `transmit` action delegating to `@io/stagefreight/narrative` at the
# wire boundary. The isomorphism IS altitude-portable:
#
#   temporal narrative (@song/narrative)  ⇔  symphonic narrative (@mirror/spectral)
#                    ⇩ transmit                              ⇩ project
#   wire narrative (@io/stagefreight/narrative)  ⇔  narratable prose (@docblock)
#
# The wire↔symphonic isomorphism at StageFreight cascade altitude
# (audition/perform/review/publish/narrate ⇔ exposition/development/
# recapitulation ⇔ song-form) IS a candidate #S4 (provisional; per Seam
# Phase D TICK 4 audit `d2d511b`): the substrate has been carrying the
# same bounded-frame-shift discipline at wire, symphonic, and temporal
# altitudes; this species names the wire↔temporal composition explicitly
# at the transmit boundary. The wire↔symphonic altitude-portable
# discipline IS the narrative's structural anchor at wire altitude.
# Absorption of provisional #S4 into #S3 (five-op temporal specialisation)
# is naming-refinement, not new recognition; Pack adjudication at Seam
# Phase D.
